Acceptance criteria
-------------------
The entire 3:2 game picture and surrounding black bezel/monochrome wordmark fit
at 100%, with dark unused space. Shrinking retains both aspect ratios and does
not move, restart, pause or restore the native runtime. Controls remain visible
outside the bezel; the slider accepts keyboard/touch/pointer input without
stealing game controls when the actual LCD is focused. Escape and close work.

Completion evidence
-------------------
Existing fullscreen used a full-size canvas inside an intrinsic grid track,
which could exceed its container height. Replaced that layout with a definite
viewport-sized, min-size-zero flex container and a proportional fitted stage.
The fullscreen bezel is a lightweight CSS presentation matching physical
surround/LCD proportions; it is not a second rendering of the whole 3D room.
The actual native framebuffer remains copied in full, without ROM-specific
cropping, and the original runtime/3D desk remain in place.
Expanded actual native quick-action case passes Edge44.1s and explicit
Chromium/SwiftShader1.4m, including exact live pixels/input, refusal recovery,
both exits and unchanged runtime/save/autosave/restart checks.
Fit and zoom checked at1920x1080,844x390,390x844,320x568: full bezel above
controls,3:2 LCD, correct50% width/height and keyboard range changes.
Reviewed actual desktop/phone/50% captures. No new user aesthetic approval
or physical-device qualification is inferred.

